# Stripe webhook ops (PinOnIt)

Endpoint (live): `https://adlusgtlwgcfyxgeoias.supabase.co/functions/v1/stripe-webhook`  
Preferred destination name in Stripe: **`engaging-sensation`** (keep **one** active destination only).

## Deploy (required)

Stripe sends **no** `Authorization` header. Always:

```bash
supabase functions deploy stripe-webhook --no-verify-jwt --project-ref adlusgtlwgcfyxgeoias
```

Or run `./scripts/deploy-edge-functions.sh` (includes `--no-verify-jwt` for stripe-webhook).

Never deploy `stripe-webhook` without `--no-verify-jwt`. Gateway JWT → `Missing authorization header` → Stripe disables the endpoint.

## Signature verify (Deno)

Use `await stripe.webhooks.constructEventAsync(...)` — never sync `constructEvent` (SubtleCrypto 400s every event).

## Secret hygiene

- Supabase Edge secret name: **`STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`** (`whsec_…`).
- Each Stripe destination has its **own** signing secret.
- After creating, rotating, or switching destinations: immediately update `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` to match that destination. No redeploy needed after secret change.
- Do **not** keep two destinations to the same URL (two secrets → signature mismatches).

## Monitoring

- `health-monitor` probes Stripe Webhook (JWT gate / SubtleCrypto / missing-signature OK).
- Set `HEALTH_ALERT_PHONE` in Supabase for SMS when health checks fail.
- Remind the user to enable Stripe webhook failure emails and keep a single Active destination.

## After webhook outages

Remind: Resend failed Stripe events; open Billing (calls `syncStripeSubscription`) to heal plan badges.
